# SRS & Practice

## SRS model

- **Not** SM-2/Anki — multi-track Leitner per `(word, channel)`
- **4 channels**: meaning, listening, pinyin, sentence
- Intervals in `src/config/constants.ts`: `CN_SRS_INTERVAL_DAYS` (1d → 30d ladder)
- All channels active from enrollment (`channelRamp.ts` stub returns true)
- First wrong on MCQ stages: 30m cooldown (`CN_WRONG_FIRST_RETRY_MINUTES`)
- Sentence channel due only when word has fill-ready `CnExample` rows (`loadWordIdsWithFillExamples`)
- Due eligibility: schedule only — **no** lifetime-rate weak bypass in `isChannelDue`

## Due query perf

- SQL superset prefilter: `buildDueCandidateWhere` in `cnSrsDueQuery.ts` (includes `sentenceDueAt`)
- JS `isChannelDue` remains source of truth
- Indexes on `userId + *DueAt` per channel

## Practice

- **11 core question types** — `coreQuestionTypes.ts` (includes `fill_sentence`, `fill_sentence_typed`)
- Sentence ladder: mcq1/mcq2 → `fill_sentence` MCQ; recall/maintain → `fill_sentence_typed`
- Examples: 5 `vi_du_1…5` per word in `tu_vung` import (`parseFillExample.ts`)
- Question generation: `generateQuestions.ts` + `verifiedExample.ts`
- Modes: `core_vocab`, `listening`, `sentence`, `smart_mixed`

## Tests

- SRS logic: `src/lib/__tests__/cnSrsService.test.ts`
- Ramp: `src/lib/__tests__/channelRamp.test.ts`
